@startuml state-active-page
!include elvira.iuml
' What: in the continuous view the active page is set by scrolling or by a jump, never both at once, so a jump never loops back through the scroll handler. Drawing no longer pins the page: since #156 every page has its own ink layer, saved under its own page number.
' Kind: UML state machine diagram. Scope: who may change docStore.activePage in the PageStream.
' Source: src/stores/document.ts, src/components/pdf-viewer-page/PageStream.vue, src/stores/ink.ts (2026-11-18)

title Who owns the active page

[*] --> Following : document opened (cause: initial)

state Following : the page nearest the top of the view\nbecomes active (cause: scroll, no history)
state Jumping : goTo(page, cause) scrolls the stream there;\nscroll updates are ignored until it settles

Following --> Jumping : link · outline · search · citation · host · history · step
Jumping --> Following : scroll settled on the target

caption Scrolling only reports (cause scroll, no history entry); jumps scroll and are recorded. Drawing does not depend on the active page.
footer ELVIRA · FIIT STU · EvilFlowersViewer · docs/diagrams/state-active-page.puml
@enduml
